  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Checking for Sheets Reference**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `/skills` directory to confirm the existence of the Google Sheets integration reference, as mentioned in the documentation. I need to verify that `/skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/references/sheets.md` or a similar file is actually present before proceeding further.\n\n\n**Investigating Sheets Integration**\n\nI\'m now shifting focus to the Google Sheets API. I\'ve identified the necessary endpoint for querying sheet data: `https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/{spreadsheetId}/values/{range}` (GET method, Bearer token authentication). I\'ve also confirmed that the `spreadsheets.readonly` scope is the minimum required to read spreadsheet values, which is exactly what I need. The next step is to figure out the best way to utilize the provided Google Sheet as a data source.\n\n\n**Considering OAuth Setup**\n\nI\'m now grappling with the OAuth requirement for accessing the public Google Sheet. The instructions are clear: I must use `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: false`. The user needs to confirm the OAuth setup in LINE. The challenge is balancing the OAuth requirement with the goal of minimizing friction for users viewing the equipment status in the LINE webview. I am now evaluating the best flow for integrating this with the LINE setup.\n\n\n**Evaluating Authentication Options**\n\nI am now carefully considering the authentication approach. Since the Google Sheets integration mandates the Workspace Skill, OAuth is required. However, I\'m exploring fetching the data as a public CSV using an API Key. While this sidesteps OAuth, the instructions clearly specify that the Google Workspace integration must be used, which means OAuth must be implemented. My goal is to determine the optimal workflow for this integration, considering the requirements and the user experience.\n\n\n"
