  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Architecture Choices**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the architecture for this project. I\'m leaning toward a full-stack approach, incorporating both a server and client. Specifically, I\'m considering using Express for the backend. The key is to create server-side API routes, and to secure all API keys, like the Gemini API key, from the client-side.\n\n\n**Confirming Architectural Advantage**\n\nMy recent thinking leans even further toward a full-stack Express approach. Fetching public Google Sheets data becomes effortless, bypassing CORS issues. This architecture ensures API key security, and makes deployment simple. I\'m especially excited about this as it lets me fetch the spreadsheet data, parse it, and serve it. Now, I need to confirm the spreadsheet doesn\'t have other sheets.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve decided on the core API endpoints. I\'ll build a server (`server.ts`) to handle sheet data. I\'ll include `/api/sheets/public` for direct public CSV retrieval, `/api/sheets/metadata` for metadata access (using an access token or public data), and `/api/sheets/values` for fetching specific sheet values using an access token. Now, I\'m thinking about a highly polished UI.\n\n\n**Designing UI/UX**\n\nMy focus is shifting to UI/UX now, thinking about visual elements for a dashboard design. I\'m aiming for accessibility with target elements of at least 44px, using modern fonts, and a cohesive light theme. I\'m envisioning two main views, or a tabbed unified view for mobile. The first view will be a \"Gear Status Dashboard\", showcasing rental and stock stats with a searchable list. I\'m now considering the ideal columns to include: Life jacket, Butt pad, and Paddles (carbon and wooden).\n\n\n**Calculating Inventory Statistics**\n\nI\'m now calculating item statistics for the inventory. Specifically, I\'m working out \"currently borrowed\" counts for each gear type like paddles and life jackets. To calculate the remaining inventory correctly, I need to know the total inventory, so I\'ll let users configure this value within the app. I think it would be great to calculate these stats and provide a polished UI!\n\n\n**Adding AI Recommendation**\n\nI\'m now integrating an AI-powered gear recommendation feature. I\'ll implement a server-side Gemini chat to assist users with gear selection based on their height, weight, and skill level, offering tailored recommendations and acquisition paths. This feature will include info on buying, renting, and group buys. Additionally, I\'ll add instant keyword search to filter gear. I plan to read through `src/App.tsx` and design the file structure with types, and static data.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/types.ts` to declare the TypeScript types for the application\'s gear, rentals, inventory, and AI messages."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 12355119
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
