  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Deployment Options**\n\nI\'m exploring the possibility of deploying this to GitHub, alongside transforming the React frontend into a static, \"Listen to the Web\"-esque site. My focus is on the \"Fetch\" button interaction, with a clearer vision of what this transition would entail.\n\n\n**Analyzing Architectural Trade-offs**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the architectural implications of a GitHub Pages deployment. It\'s becoming clear that a static site won\'t support the Express backend. This means the Gemini API key needs careful handling. The current full-stack approach, with APIs for Sheets and AI, is not compatible with pure static hosting. I\'m strategizing how to keep functionality.\n\n\n**Evaluating Security Risks**\n\nI\'ve realized that putting the API key on the client-side is a big no-no. It opens me up to security risks and the potential for abuse and costs. Direct calls to Google Sheets from the client side are tricky too. Public sheets might face CORS restrictions, and while OAuth sheets can work, the AI Coach Advisor (Gemini) still requires server-side handling.\n\n\n**Addressing Security Concerns**\n\nI\'ve got a clearer picture now. The Gemini API key means I need a server-side route. GitHub Pages won\'t work alone. I\'m exploring serverless options like Cloud Run, Vercel, Render, or Netlify Functions to keep the key safe. I am thinking of a proxy, and the AI Coach might need a backend now.\n\n\n**Investigating Hosting Alternatives**\n\nI am now thoroughly evaluating alternative hosting options that could provide a robust solution. I have identified **CORS restrictions** as a key challenge; the existing Express backend cleverly bypasses this. Client-side Google Sheets API access for **custom spreadsheets** looks workable with OAuth. Vercel, Netlify, or Cloud Run are looking like promising full-stack alternatives to GitHub Pages.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "\351\200\231\346\230\257\344\270\200\345\200\213\351\235\236\345\270\270\346\243\222\344\270\224\345\213\231\345\257\246\347\232\204\346\203\263\346\263\225\357\274\201\345\260\207 React \345\211\215\347\253\257\345\201\232\346\210\220\344\270\200\345\200\213\347\264\224\351\235\234\346\205\213\347\232\204\345\226\256\351\240\201\346\207\211\347\224\250\347\250\213\345\274\217\357\274\210SPA\357\274\211\357\274\214\344\270\246\351\200\217\351\201\216\346\211\213\345\213\225\351\273\236\346\223\212\343\200\214\351\207\215\346\226\260\346\225\264\347\220\206 / \345\220\214\346\255\245\343\200\215\346\231\202\346\211\215\351\200\217\351\201\216\347\200\217\350\246\275\345\231\250\347\233\264\346\216\245\345\220\221 Google \351\200\262\350\241\214 Web API \350\253\213\346\261\202\357\274\214\347\242\272\345\257\246\345\217\257\344\273\245\350\256\223\346\210\221\345\200\221\345\260\207\345\205\266\351\203\250\347\275\262\345\234\250 **GitHub Pages** \351\200\231\351\241\236\345\205\215\350\262\273\347\232\204\351\235\234\346\205\213\344\270\273\351\240\201\347\251\272\351\226\223\344\270\212\343\200\202\n\n\347\204\266\350\200\214\357\274\214\345\234\250\346\261\272\345\256\232\345\205\250\351\235\242\346\224\271\347\202\272\347\264\224\345\211\215\347\253\257\346\236\266\346\247\213\357\274\210GitHub Pages \351\203\250\347\275\262\357\274\211\344\271\213\345\211\215\357\274\214\346\234\211\345\271\276\345\200\213**\351\227\234\351\215\265\347\232\204\346\212\200\350\241\223\351\231\220\345\210\266\350\210\207\346\236\266\346\247\213\345\256\211\345\205\250\350\200\203\351\207\217**\351\234\200\350\246\201\350\210\207\346\202\250\345\210\206\344\272\253\357\274\232\n\n---\n\n### 1. \346\240\270\345\277\203\351\231\220\345\210\266\357\274\232AI \346\225\231\347\267\264\350\253\256\350\251\242\357\274\210Gemini API\357\274\211\347\232\204\345\256\211\345\205\250\351\242\250\351\232\252\n\351\200\231\346\230\257\346\234\200\351\227\234\351\215\265\3