    thinking: "**Analyzing API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the backend API endpoints. I have `/api/sheets/public` for parsing public CSVs, and `/api/sheets/custom` for authenticated sheets. There\'s also `/api/ai/recommend` which feeds the Gemini model. Wait, the user wants me to do something with the react frontend.\n\n\n**Refactoring to Client-Side**\n\nI\'m shifting the architecture significantly. The goal is a more static website. My current plan involves moving all data fetching to the client-side React app. The public sheet will directly fetch and parse CSV data. The custom sheet will use the browser\'s `fetch` API with OAuth for Google Sheets data. This should make GitHub Pages deployment feasible.\n\n\n**Enhancing AI Integration**\n\nI\'m now exploring client-side AI options. My priority is a zero-latency local rules advisor, fully functional offline and on static sites. For advanced users, I\'ll add optional Gemini API key input. This will allow them to integrate Gemini directly from the client. Alternatively, a Gemini SDK client-side integration will be provided, if desired, to further enhance the local AI advisor with smart functionality.\n\n\n"
