    thinking: "**Considering AI Coach Options**\n\nI\'m evaluating strategies for disabling the AI coach feature. Currently, I\'m leaning toward implementing a boolean variable for straightforward control. Alternatively, dynamically hiding the \"Coach Consultation\" tab seems promising, offering immediate visual control. Further, I can conditionally display it or filter out elements to manage the feature.\n\n\n**Refining Disable Strategies**\n\nI\'m now focusing on disabling the AI coach by default, as requested. Hiding the \"Coach Consultation\" tab initially and introducing an \"Enable AI Coach\" toggle in the header seems optimal. Considering the app\'s structure, I think a simple toggle would be a clean solution, though I can alternatively hide the tab completely unless enabled. I\'ll evaluate the implementation\'s impact, considering UI structure.\n\n\n**Exploring Enable/Disable**\n\nI\'m now thinking about directly disabling the AI Consultant tab by default. I can introduce a setting or a toggle to enable it, perhaps labeled \"\345\225\237\347\224\250 AI \346\225\231\347\267\264\345\212\237\350\203\275\" (Enable AI Coach Feature) in the navigation. This approach offers control and flexibility.\n\n\n**Implementing Default Hiding**\n\nI\'m now implementing the default hiding strategy. The goal is to disable the AI Coach by default, as the user requested, and I\'m currently leaning towards implementing a toggle. I plan to use `localStorage` to save the user\'s preference for the AI Coach. My approach involves using `localStorage.getItem(\'enable_ai_coach\') === \'true\'` to check the state, which is simple, and setting the toggle as hidden by default. I\'ll integrate an \"Show AI Coach Consultant\" setting within the Custom Spreadsheet Connection section. This will be controlled by a simple boolean, initially set to `false`, and I\'m exploring integration in `src/App.tsx`.\n\n\n"
